  <body>
    <pre><span class="hdr">404(1)                         User Commands                        404(1)</span>

<b>NAME</b>
       404 - the resource you requested does not exist

<b>SYNOPSIS</b>
       GET &lt;that-thing-you-wanted&gt;

<b>DESCRIPTION</b>
       The  file, directory, or resource you were looking for could not
       be located on this server. It may have been moved, deleted,
       renamed, or perhaps it never existed in the first place.

       Please remain calm and try one of the following:

       *  Double-check the URL for typos
       *  Consult the directory listing at the mirror root
       *  Accept this as a sign to go outside for a bit

<b>EXIT STATUS</b>
       404 Not Found.

<b>BUGS</b>
       Probably. This page is one of them.

<b>SEE ALSO</b>
       index(1), rsync(1), the actual <a href="/">mirror list</a>

<span class="hdr">Linux Kernel Archives          2026-07-06                           404(1)</span></pre>
